<<~ ahu #/head>>

! CompositeStore ~ many layers, one reading

Layers stack lowest to highest. A title standing in several bags resolves to the highest-priority bag
that holds it — ''standard TW5 recipe law, unchanged'', so an operator who knows TiddlyWiki already
knows this one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The invariants

# ''READS fan out; the highest priority answers.'' A get or a visible-list consults every layer and
returns the topmost holder.
# ''WRITES route to ONE designated store.'' A put or a tombstone lands in the writable bag — the wiki
layer by default — and never scatters across the stack. A write that chose its layer by lookup would
mutate whichever bag happened to answer the read.
# ''A subscriber MUST read the change's ORIGIN.'' Subscription fans out to every layer, so a caller
that ignored origin would hear its own write echo back and act on it again.
# ''A layer MAY arrive after construction.'' Corpus islands land async, so the stack grows while the
store already serves reads.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-ordering-hazard>>

!! Subscribe BEFORE the layer arrives

A layer added after construction begins emitting the moment it lands. ''A caller that subscribes
afterward misses every change the layer carried in with it'' — and a missed arrival looks exactly like a
layer that held nothing.

Two orderings answer it, and a caller takes one deliberately: subscribe first and let the arrival
flow through, or add the layer and then force a refresh once it returns. ''Doing neither reads as an
empty bag rather than as a missed window'' — the failure this note exists to name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

